  "ethnobotanical_info": "Māori traditionally used Karo’s dense, durable wood to make tools, weapons, and musical instruments, and the plant was also used as a source of natural dye. Its highly fragrant flowers hold cultural significance in Māori tradition and have been associated with love and romance.",
